    "physical_description": null,
    "summary": "Dogon masks can be interpreted on two fundamentally different levels: “front speech” (<em>giri so</em>) reflects an early stage of knowledge and consists of a tale that is intended to arouse curiosity; and “speech of the world” (<em>aduno so</em>) refers to Dogon cosmogony, reserved for highly instructed men and women. Masked dances have recently been organized in Dogon regions for tourists and dignitaries. The character of <em>omono</em> is a rare one among the 80 or so that appear in Dogon masquerades.",
